  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Impact Cluster: PoultryTechUganda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to create a resilient and profitable Ugandan poultry value chain, through substituting imported farming inputs with locally produced inputs, allowing for broad sustainable development of Ugandan poultry farmers.This project will improve the position of the small and medium-size poultry farmers in Uganda, a growing group in the country. This group is still highly dependent on imported Day Old Chicks (DOC), because local players do not currently produce at the same level. The reliance on imported DOCs means a significant cost increase for these farmers, as well as a business risk in terms of reliability of supply. Moreover, this group can significantly improve their performance and efficiency by applying better farming practices, especially on the topics of treating chicks in the first life stages (heating and water), nutrition and animal health/biosecurity.The project goal is to improve overall productivity, sustainability and resilience in the Ugandan poultry value chain, while strengthening business relationships between the Dutch and Ugandan cluster members and thus increase overall investment in the value chain.</narrative>
  </description>
